<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hussein Dey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1765–<a href="/years/1838">1838</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hussein Dey (c. 1765–1838) was the last dey of the Regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, ruling from 1818 to 1830. In 1827, during a dispute over debts owed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> for grain, he struck the French consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-deval">Pierre Deval</a> with a fly-whisk, giving France a pretext for a naval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a>. When the French invaded in 1830 he surrendered Algiers and went into exile, dying in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hussein-dey.jpg" alt="Hussein Dey" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: German inscription · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dey_Hussein_Pacha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
